          "settings": {
            "show_number": true,
            "heading": "ADHD Isn’t a Willpower Problem",
            "text": "<h2><strong>It’s a Dopamine Signal Problem.<br/><br/></strong></h2><p>You don’t struggle because you’re lazy.<br/><br/>You struggle because your brain doesn’t fire the “start” signal reliably.</p><p>You know what to do.<br/><br/>You want to do it.<br/><br/>But nothing moves.</p><p>Without stable dopamine, intention never turns into action.</p><p>This isn’t about trying harder.<br/><br/>It’s about a signal that isn’t strong enough.</p>",
            "media_type": "image",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
        "media_text_block_FiKwxb": {
          "type": "media_text_block",
          "settings": {
            "show_number": true,
            "heading": "ADHD Motivation Comes in Bursts",
            "text": "<h2><strong>And Disappears Just as Fast.<br/><br/></strong></h2><p>Some days you feel unstoppable.<br/><br/>Clear. Driven. Locked in.</p><p>Then it’s gone.</p><p>Not slowly. Instantly.</p><p>That’s the dopamine spike-and-crash cycle.</p><p>Consistency feels impossible<br/><br/>because your motivation isn’t stable.</p><p>And without stability, nothing sticks.</p>",
            "media_type": "image",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
        "media_text_block_PBHRkq": {
          "type": "media_text_block",
          "settings": {
            "show_number": true,
            "heading": "Low Dopamine Makes Everything Heavier",
            "text": "<h2><strong>Focus, Time, and Emotions All Break Down</strong><br/><br/>Simple tasks feel overwhelming.<br/><br/>Time slips away without warning.<br/><br/>Your thoughts scatter.</h2><p>You try to push through.<br/><br/>Your emotions spike.<br/><br/>You shut down.</p>",
            "media_type": "image",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
        "media_text_block_DfcqPh": {
          "type": "media_text_block",
          "settings": {
            "show_number": true,
            "heading": "Why Most ADHD Solutions Fall Apart",
            "text": "<h2><strong>They Rely on the One Thing ADHD Can’t Provide</strong><br/><br/>Routines rely on memory.<br/><br/>Systems rely on energy.<br/><br/>Habits rely on consistency.</h2><p>On good days they work.<br/><br/>On low-dopamine days they collapse.</p><p>More pressure doesn’t fix this.<br/><br/>Less friction does.</p>",
            "media_type": "image",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
